Benchmark examples inside the optimized prompts
  The few-shot demos in src/agents_gym_core/agents/<benchmark>/prompts/miprov2/*.json (40 in
  10 files) quote training examples of their benchmarks, under the benchmarks' licences:
  - HotpotQA and HoVer: questions, claims and Wikipedia abstracts. CC BY-SA 4.0.
  - IFBench: prompts. ODC-BY 1.0.
  - PUPA: user queries. MIT.
  The AIME and LiveBench-Math demos quote no benchmark text: their predict.refs.json files name
  the datapoint of each problem and solution, and gym init fills the text in from the downloaded
  datasets. A few GEPA prompts (hotpotqa/prompts/{gepa__gpt-4.1-mini,gepa__qwen3.5-122b,
  gepa__qwen3.5-9b}/, hover/prompts/gepa__gpt-5/, papillon/prompts/gepa__gpt-5/) also quote
  individual HotpotQA questions, HoVer claims and PUPA queries, under the same licences.

Apart from those quotations, the public benchmarks' datasets are not part of this repository: gym
init downloads them, and IFBench's files come with the gepa-artifact submodule. Their sources and licences are listed
in docs/REPRODUCING.md.
